course: dictionary
lesson: 13843
title: An old spelling: jigg
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes a word looks strange because it is spelled in an old way. Old books and songs may write «jigg» with two g's. Jigg is not a standard English word today, so you will not find it as a normal word in a modern dictionary. Read it as «jig» instead.
explain: A jig is a quick, bouncy dance, often Irish or Scottish, and also the lively tune played for it. «The fiddler played a jigg, and the children jumped about the floor.» Here jigg means jig. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
explain: Jigg can also be the start of a longer word that was cut off, like «jiggle». When you meet jigg, look at the letters around it and at the whole sentence before you decide what it means.
fact: Jigg is an old or misspelt form of «jig».
fact: «Jig» means a lively, bouncy dance, often Irish or Scottish, or the tune for it.
fact: «To jig» means to dance or bounce about quickly.
fact: Jigg may also be part of a longer word, such as «jiggle».
fact: When a spelling looks odd, read it as the nearest word you know, then check it in the sentence.
exercise: In an old song, «The fiddler played a jigg for the dancers.» What does jigg mean here? | A large, heavy stone | A slow, sad lullaby | A kind of wooden boat | *A lively, bouncy dance or its tune
exercise: Old books spell it «jigg». Which everyday word should you read it as? | *Jig | Jaw | Jug | Jump
exercise: «The jelly began to jiggle on the plate.» Which meaning fits jiggle best? | Melt away quietly | Sing loudly | *Shake or move quickly from side to side | Freeze solid
test: «The dancers began a merry jig at the fair.» What does jig mean? | A type of cake | *A quick, bouncy dance | A long, quiet walk | Stuck, unable to move
test: Why might a modern reader find «jigg» puzzling? | *It is an old spelling and not a standard English word | It is a word from the Moon | It is spelled the same way today | It means the same as sleep
exam: A child reads «The old book said the band played a jigg all night.» What should the child do to understand jigg? | Skip the whole sentence and never read on | Look it up as a sea creature | *Read it as jig, a lively dance, and check that the sentence makes sense | Guess it means a cold drink
